Z||000012||Predator||04-02-2001||08:07 PM||||Hey Cliff try MusicMatch. It will convert from MP3 to WAV and from WAV to MP3. Also it is a nice player. <A HREF="http://www.musicmatch.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.musicmatch.com</A>  You can use it for free or buy the upgrade. The conversion works with the free version. Oh yea I played the Guitar way back. I haven't played in years though. Used to play Southern Rock. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Predator (edited 04-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cliff Pennock||04-03-2001||06:19 AM||||That makes me soooo angry... I downloaded MusicMatch Jukebox because on the website it said it's the only free program that includes MP3 encoding. Well, I install it and when I try to encode a WAV to MP3, I get a pop-up screen saying "this feature is only available in the Plus version"!<P>This happens almost every time I download a program that pretends to be free. Yesterday I downloaded another "free" encoder. On the website it said it was freeware and after installation, it turned out to be a crippled version of a non-free program, with almost every feature disabled (including MP3 encoding). Live and learn I guess.||||reg||8
